signals

A signal is a message sent by the OS or a running application to our program. It is sent to indicate that a significant event has occurred

kill-l  Lists all the available signals

pgrep -a terminal
pgrep -a bash
id
kill -2 id
kill -l 


Trapping Signals

When a running process is interrupted, it might get aborted even before completing clean ups.
So, you may end up leaving a bunch of temporary files that won't get cleaned up. Trapping
these signals are easy and a good way to deal with it.

